ExGr5PV8", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["compensate_partial", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379405, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Uq8zUDMDTZWmzRExGr5PV8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383291, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #102 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s comment says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So `2.665` came out as `2.67`, while the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On the branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I switched `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`). That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #102, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/102\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QjHUF2kz7A5GRyXeWA5n6j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KdCjzLcTyBAcLL9dFipr9u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FreeyQW3LYZ1ZAtsjobnTA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011Htcs3MqejTUtiGRcZDfzF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason":